// The written clocks of := (kbak/clafer-semantics#194): := each initializes each instance at
// its birth, and := together the instances under a parent at its birth (all the instances of
// a top-level abstract clafer at time zero), whatever the multiplicity.
// In a static model, which has a single state, := each is an equation for each instance: both
// instances of xs have the value 1, and each of V has 5. := together is one equation for all
// the instances: the values of ys are 1 and 2 together.

xs ->> integer 2 := each 1
ys ->> integer 2 := together 1, 2

abstract Val ->> integer 0..3 := each 5
V : Val 2
